    <h2 id="who">1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      XHOCK is organised by KOA Sports ("KOA", "we", "us"), a private, independent organisation focused on
      sports experiences and athlete development. XHOCK is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or represented by
      any national or international hockey federation.
    </p>
    <p>
      Legal entity, registered address and tax identification: <strong>[KOA to confirm]</strong>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="tickets">2. Tickets and what they include</h2>
    <p>
      The product sold on this page is a <strong>Player Ticket</strong> priced at <strong>{{ event.price }} {{ event.currency }}</strong> per
      player. A Player Ticket includes:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Participation in the XHOCK tournament (round robin format).</li>
      <li>Assignment to a team by XHOCK, including for individual registrations.</li>
      <li>The commemorative jersey and the activities and additional experiences described on the tickets page.</li>
      <li>Access to the venue during the event for the registered player.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      A Player Ticket does <strong>not</strong> include travel, lodging, meals, transfers, insurance, equipment
      or companion access, unless a specific inclusion is stated in writing at the time of purchase. Companion
      access and hotel rates are subject to the conditions confirmed by KOA.
    </p>
    <p>
      The maximum number of tickets per order is <strong>10</strong>. The website enforces this limit and the
      server must enforce it again.
    </p>

    <h2 id="registration">3. Registration and eligibility</h2>
    <p>
      The person completing the purchase must be at least 18 years old and is responsible for the accuracy of
      the contact details and of every player's information (name, age, position and jersey size).
    </p>
    <p>
      Players under 18 may only participate with the authorisation of a parent or legal guardian, who must
      complete the registration on their behalf. The minimum registered age is 5 and the maximum is 99;
      exceptions require written approval from KOA.
    </p>
    <p>
      Team assignment, roster size, positions and schedule are decided by KOA. Registering with friends does
      not guarantee being placed on the same team.
    </p>

    <h2 id="payment">4. Price, payment and taxes</h2>
    <p>
      Prices are shown in US dollars (USD). Payment is processed by <strong>Stripe</strong> on Stripe-hosted
      checkout pages. KOA does not receive or store full card numbers.
    </p>
    <p>
      The final amount, including any applicable taxes or processing fees, is the amount displayed on the
      Stripe checkout page before you confirm the payment. Currency conversion, if your card is issued in
      another currency, is handled by your bank.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your order is confirmed when Stripe reports a successful payment. The confirmation email is sent to the
      address you entered in the form.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">5. Changes, cancellation and refunds</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>[KOA to confirm]</strong> — the refund, transfer and cancellation policy must be defined and
      published here before ticket sales are promoted. It should cover at least:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Voluntary cancellation by the player and the applicable deadline.</li>
      <li>Whether a ticket can be transferred to another player, and how.</li>
      <li>What happens if KOA cancels or postpones the event.</li>
      <li>What happens if the schedule, venue or format changes.</li>
      <li>How refunds are requested and how long they take.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Until that policy is published, any request must be made in writing through the contact channel in
      section 11 and will be reviewed case by case by KOA.
    </p>
    <p>
      KOA may change the schedule, venue, format or activities for operational, safety or force majeure
      reasons. Material changes will be communicated to the email address used at purchase.
    </p>

    <h2 id="conduct">6. Conduct, safety and risk</h2>
    <p>
      Ice hockey is a contact sport. By registering, players acknowledge the inherent risk of injury and
      agree to follow the rules of the tournament, the instructions of referees and staff, and the safety
      rules of Happi Arena Cancun.
    </p>
    <p>
      Players are responsible for bringing their own equipment and for ensuring it is in safe condition.
      KOA may remove any participant who behaves dangerously, discriminates against others, or breaches
      venue rules, without refund where the applicable policy allows it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Travel and medical insurance are the responsibility of each participant. <strong>[KOA to confirm:
      whether medical coverage or a waiver is required.]</strong>
    </p>

    <h2 id="media">7. Photography and media</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>[KOA to confirm]</strong> — KOA intends to photograph and record the event for communication
      and promotional purposes. The final policy, including how participants (or the guardians of minors)
      can opt out, must be approved before publication.
    </p>

    <h2 id="ip">8. Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The XHOCK and KOA names, logos, photographs, videos and page content are owned by KOA or used with
      permission. They may not be reproduced for commercial purposes without written authorisation.
    </p>

    <h2 id="liability">9. Liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, KOA is not liable for indirect or consequential
      losses, or for travel, accommodation or other costs incurred by participants beyond the price of the
      ticket. Nothing in these terms excludes liability that cannot legally be excluded.
    </p>

    <h2 id="law">10. Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>[KOA to confirm]</strong> — these terms are intended to be governed by the laws of the United
      Mexican States and the courts of Quintana Roo, Mexico, without prejudice to mandatory consumer
      protections in the buyer's country of residence.
    </p>

